<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-8 py-20">
<h2 class="font-headline text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-10 tracking-tighter">San Diego stuff worth knowing</h2>
<div class="space-y-6">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold mb-2">The city's free bulky pickup</h3>
<p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">City of San Diego Environmental Services gives each household <strong>one free bulky-item pickup per year</strong>. If you have a single item (one mattress, one couch) and you can wait 2 to 4 weeks, schedule through the <a href="https://www.sandiego.gov/environmental-services/collection/bulkypickup" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary underline">city's bulky pickup form</a>. Free beats $125. For anything larger or faster, call us.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold mb-2">Parking and the side-street access problem</h3>
<p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Older SD neighborhoods (North Park, South Park, Hillcrest, Golden Hill) were laid out for Model Ts. Our trailer is 12 feet long on a 3/4-ton truck. If your street is narrow, a permit-parking zone, or has a street-sweep schedule that morning, flag it when you text. We'll plan for it.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg font-bold mb-2">HOA &amp; condo requirements</h3>
<p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Downtown highrises and Mission Valley condos often require a certificate of insurance (COI) and proof of licensure before work. Mention your building when you text and we'll email the COI before we arrive. Some buildings also require service-elevator reservations; give us lead time.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

